# Hosts and URL shapes that lychee must not report on.
#
# Each entry is a regex matched against the whole URL. Only add a host here if
# it is *hostile to bots* rather than actually broken -- an entry here means we
# stop hearing about that link forever, so a genuinely dead link hidden behind
# one of these patterns will never be caught.

# --- Bot-hostile / anti-scraping (verified 403 or challenge page to non-browsers) ---
# Slack's invite endpoint answers 403 to anything without a browser fingerprint.
^https?://slack\.opalrb\.com
# Cloudflare-fronted Q&A sites: 403/503 to datacenter IPs.
^https?://(www\.)?stackoverflow\.com
^https?://(www\.)?stackexchange\.com
^https?://(meta\.)?stackoverflow\.com

# --- Rate limiters (429 under CI's shared egress IPs) ---
^https?://(www\.)?opencollective\.com
^https?://(www\.)?patreon\.com
^https?://(www\.)?bountysource\.com
^https?://(www\.)?reddit\.com
^https?://(www\.)?twitter\.com
^https?://(www\.)?x\.com
^https?://(www\.)?linkedin\.com

# --- Shields/badge endpoints: dynamic SVG, frequently 429, never "documentation" ---
^https?://img\.shields\.io
^https?://badge\.fury\.io
^https?://badgen\.net
^https?://.*\.svg(\?.*)?$
^https?://coveralls\.io
^https?://codeclimate\.com
^https?://api\.codeclimate\.com
^https?://travis-ci\.(org|com)
^https?://github\.com/.*/(actions|workflows)/.*badge
^https?://github\.com/.*\.svg

# --- Local/example hosts that appear in code samples and are never resolvable ---
^https?://localhost
^https?://127\.0\.0\.1
^https?://0\.0\.0\.0
^https?://\[::1\]
^https?://example\.(com|org|net)
^https?://(www\.)?your-?(site|domain|app|server).*
^https?://.*\.local(/|$)
^https?://.*:(3000|4567|8000|8080|9222|9229|9292)(/|$)

# --- Template/placeholder URLs from docs prose ---
.*\{.*\}.*
.*<.*>.*
.*%7B.*
^https?://.*\.\.\..*

# --- Site-absolute paths ---
# `/docs` points at the guides index on the published opalrb.com site. With
# --root-dir set to the checkout, lychee resolves it against the repo, where
# `docs/` does exist -- so it is checked rather than ignored.

# --- GitHub blob/tree links to this repo's own files ---
# These are checked by `rake docs:links` against the working tree instead, which
# is both faster and correct on branches where the file is new.
^https?://github\.com/opal/opal/(blob|tree)/
